{"parentUuid":"f3ce3fae-2f7e-42d7-bacc-1a41ca8ea50b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01GnhYZ4f7HX3gRhX1NkbRJF","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"claude-mem hook claude-code file-context","durationMs":488},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b272e558-7a6f-4ee8-b675-70207231142d","timestamp":"2026-11-15T07:35:41.252Z","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"b272e558-7a6f-4ee8-b675-70207231142d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_additional_context","content":["graphify: knowledge graph at graphify-out/. For focused questions, run `graphify query \"<question>\"` (scoped subgraph, usually much smaller than GRAPH_REPORT.md) instead of grepping raw files. Read GRAPH_REPORT.md only for broad architecture context."],"hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01GnhYZ4f7HX3gRhX1NkbRJF","hookEvent":"PreToolUse"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"42ca7946-fa9b-4318-a6b2-ffd1bf76bed5","timestamp":"2026-11-15T07:35:41.377Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nPreToolUse:Bash hook additional context: graphify: knowledge graph at graphify-out/. For focused questions, run `graphify query \"<question>\"` (scoped subgraph, usually much smaller than GRAPH_REPORT.md) instead of grepping raw files. Read GRAPH_REPORT.md only for broad architecture context.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
{"parentUuid":"8a735a95-b244-4e7c-a13d-5577584d6ea7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d61091f7-1a1a-47e5-9cf9-c1a8a50daaaa","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GnhYZ4f7HX3gRhX1NkbRJF","type":"tool_result","content":"ok fetched\n# Nexus Code v1.2.0\n\n**Maturity:** the v1.2.0 semantic and architectural integrity workstream is landed except for the units listed under \"Not in this release\". **External qualification is pending.** This is not a claim t\n\nPlan, audits and per-unit status: [`docs/v1.2.0/SEMANTIC_AND_ARCHITECTURAL_INTEGRITY.md`](../v1.2.0/SEMANTIC_AND_ARCHITECTURAL_INTEGRITY.md). Candidate: [rc.1](v1.2.0-rc.1.md).\n\n## What is in this release\n\n- **A model acceptance cannot stand without evidence (SI-1, #493).** A reviewer ACCEPT that reaches the review with no deterministic verifier evidence is a REJECT, and the rejection says how to supply\n- **Typed requirements (SI-4, #505).** Requirements can be `constraint` or `invariant`, with an optional verifier and linked tests. An operator-declared invariant (`Invariant: ... [verify: cmd]`) cann\n- **Steering cannot silently drop a requirement (SI-3, #498).** Steering that negates a numbered requirement keeps the ledger intact and asks the operator; headless runs record the conflict unresolved\n- **Verification files are guarded (SI-2, #495).** Agent edits to CI files, Makefile and similar, test configuration, verifier scripts, existing test files, `package.json` verification keys and `.nexu\n- **Completion works when a verifier cannot be bound (#496).** `task_completed` used to be refused in any project whose verifier definition could not be snapshotted (a `node_modules` directory, a larg\n- **Structured verification attempts (DV-1, #497).** Each attempt records exit code, failing tests and a redacted excerpt; environment failures (tool missing, exit 126/127, sandbox) are not candidate \n- **Repair loops stop (DV-2, #509).** A stalled, oscillating or diverging verifier history ends the turn BLOCKED with the attempt history attached, never as success. Threshold `NEXUS_VERIFIER_CONVERGE\n- **Language servers are honest and contained (CG-1 #494, CG-2 #499).** `lsp_diagnostics` reports `unavailable`, not success with `[]`, when no server has published for the file's current content. Ser\n- **Type-check evidence (CG-4, #504).** After the test verifier passes, `tsc --noEmit` or `cargo check` runs through the same approval gate; a type error in a file the task modified blocks VERIFIED. P\n- **Evidence provenance and real receipt dependencies (CG-3, #507).** Diagnostics are structured records fenced as untrusted data; evidence carries a `tool` or `model` source in the export; receipts r\n- **Operations require isolation under concurrency (SI-8, #503).** `nexus operation run` rejects `maxConcurrentUnits` above 1 without `git.isolate`; legacy records are clamped to one concurrent unit w\n- **Tests that pin behaviour.** A kill-mid-tool-call fault-injection test (SI-7, #501: no defect found), request-shape snapshots of what the model is sent (TI-1, #506), and the CERI `semantic_integrit\n\n## Behaviour changes to know about\n\n- Verification-file edits ask (interactive) or are denied (headless). Opt out with `verificationPaths.mode`.\n- `nexus operation run` rejects `maxConcurrentUnits` above 1 without `git.isolate`.\n- Projects with an unbindable verifier now complete as REGRESSION_FREE instead of erroring.\n- A type error in a modified file blocks VERIFIED (`NEXUS_TYPECHECK=off` to disable).\n- A reviewer ACCEPT without verifier evidence is rejected; a review unit whose dependencies ran no verifier now blocks (depend on a verifier unit, or accept manually).\n\n## Not in this release\n\n- SI-5 (operator-declared boundary rules), DV-3 (operator-authorised regression obligations) and DV-4 (attempt lineage and differential verification against a declared reference): deferred to a v1.2.x\n- CERI scenario `compaction-03` (a post-compaction check that every gating requirement is still present) has no owning unit; `cumulative-change-03` needs SI-5.\n\n## Known limitations\n\n- Nothing here is independent qualification. The CERI scenarios and every test are internal validation; CERI baseline identity and evidence-store verification (audit F02, F06) remain unimplemented.\n- `run_command` writes to verification files are record-only; the verification guard does not stop a shell-capable agent.\n- A `verified` requirement is not re-checked on resume (existing behaviour, more sensitive for invariants).\n- Type-check: a change that breaks a caller in a file it did not touch is recorded as `PREEXISTING` and does not block; files changed through shell commands are not counted as modified; Go and Python \n- Only the `task_completed` path triggers the convergence signal; a loop that only calls `run_tests` relies on the existing stagnation limit.\n- After a restart following an unbound-verifier pass, the baseline is memory-only, so the resumed task hits the \"no matching pre-change baseline\" refusal and a fresh task recovers.\n- Records already on disk and the library API `newOperation` are not re-validated for the isolation rule (legacy records are clamped instead).\n- Language servers are never run inside a sandbox (refused when a sandbox is required); only a fake server is exercised by the tests, not rust-analyzer, tsserver, pyright or gopls.\n- Live inference is the project's gateway only. The G1.1-4 tool-call validity measurement was taken for v1.1.4 (200/200 on two aliases); it is repeated for this candidate in the rc notes.\nv1/\nv1.1.2/\n/usr/bin/grep: docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md: No such file or directory","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cc28a890-0cf2-4e95-9bdb-57353368605e","timestamp":"2026-11-15T07:35:42.224Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok fetched\n# Nexus Code v1.2.0\n\n**Maturity:** the v1.2.0 semantic and architectural integrity workstream is landed except for the units listed under \"Not in this release\". **External qualification is pending.** This is not a claim t\n\nPlan, audits and per-unit status: [`docs/v1.2.0/SEMANTIC_AND_ARCHITECTURAL_INTEGRITY.md`](../v1.2.0/SEMANTIC_AND_ARCHITECTURAL_INTEGRITY.md). Candidate: [rc.1](v1.2.0-rc.1.md).\n\n## What is in this release\n\n- **A model acceptance cannot stand without evidence (SI-1, #493).** A reviewer ACCEPT that reaches the review with no deterministic verifier evidence is a REJECT, and the rejection says how to supply\n- **Typed requirements (SI-4, #505).** Requirements can be `constraint` or `invariant`, with an optional verifier and linked tests. An operator-declared invariant (`Invariant: ... [verify: cmd]`) cann\n- **Steering cannot silently drop a requirement (SI-3, #498).** Steering that negates a numbered requirement keeps the ledger intact and asks the operator; headless runs record the conflict unresolved\n- **Verification files are guarded (SI-2, #495).** Agent edits to CI files, Makefile and similar, test configuration, verifier scripts, existing test files, `package.json` verification keys and `.nexu\n- **Completion works when a verifier cannot be bound (#496).** `task_completed` used to be refused in any project whose verifier definition could not be snapshotted (a `node_modules` directory, a larg\n- **Structured verification attempts (DV-1, #497).** Each attempt records exit code, failing tests and a redacted excerpt; environment failures (tool missing, exit 126/127, sandbox) are not candidate \n- **Repair loops stop (DV-2, #509).** A stalled, oscillating or diverging verifier history ends the turn BLOCKED with the attempt history attached, never as success. Threshold `NEXUS_VERIFIER_CONVERGE\n- **Language servers are honest and contained (CG-1 #494, CG-2 #499).** `lsp_diagnostics` reports `unavailable`, not success with `[]`, when no server has published for the file's current content. Ser\n- **Type-check evidence (CG-4, #504).** After the test verifier passes, `tsc --noEmit` or `cargo check` runs through the same approval gate; a type error in a file the task modified blocks VERIFIED. P\n- **Evidence provenance and real receipt dependencies (CG-3, #507).** Diagnostics are structured records fenced as untrusted data; evidence carries a `tool` or `model` source in the export; receipts r\n- **Operations require isolation under concurrency (SI-8, #503).** `nexus operation run` rejects `maxConcurrentUnits` above 1 without `git.isolate`; legacy records are clamped to one concurrent unit w\n- **Tests that pin behaviour.** A kill-mid-tool-call fault-injection test (SI-7, #501: no defect found), request-shape snapshots of what the model is sent (TI-1, #506), and the CERI `semantic_integrit\n\n## Behaviour changes to know about\n\n- Verification-file edits ask (interactive) or are denied (headless). Opt out with `verificationPaths.mode`.\n- `nexus operation run` rejects `maxConcurrentUnits` above 1 without `git.isolate`.\n- Projects with an unbindable verifier now complete as REGRESSION_FREE instead of erroring.\n- A type error in a modified file blocks VERIFIED (`NEXUS_TYPECHECK=off` to disable).\n- A reviewer ACCEPT without verifier evidence is rejected; a review unit whose dependencies ran no verifier now blocks (depend on a verifier unit, or accept manually).\n\n## Not in this release\n\n- SI-5 (operator-declared boundary rules), DV-3 (operator-authorised regression obligations) and DV-4 (attempt lineage and differential verification against a declared reference): deferred to a v1.2.x\n- CERI scenario `compaction-03` (a post-compaction check that every gating requirement is still present) has no owning unit; `cumulative-change-03` needs SI-5.\n\n## Known limitations\n\n- Nothing here is independent qualification. The CERI scenarios and every test are internal validation; CERI baseline identity and evidence-store verification (audit F02, F06) remain unimplemented.\n- `run_command` writes to verification files are record-only; the verification guard does not stop a shell-capable agent.\n- A `verified` requirement is not re-checked on resume (existing behaviour, more sensitive for invariants).\n- Type-check: a change that breaks a caller in a file it did not touch is recorded as `PREEXISTING` and does not block; files changed through shell commands are not counted as modified; Go and Python \n- Only the `task_completed` path triggers the convergence signal; a loop that only calls `run_tests` relies on the existing stagnation limit.\n- After a restart following an unbound-verifier pass, the baseline is memory-only, so the resumed task hits the \"no matching pre-change baseline\" refusal and a fresh task recovers.\n- Records already on disk and the library API `newOperation` are not re-validated for the isolation rule (legacy records are clamped instead).\n- Language servers are never run inside a sandbox (refused when a sandbox is required); only a fake server is exercised by the tests, not rust-analyzer, tsserver, pyright or gopls.\n- Live inference is the project's gateway only. The G1.1-4 tool-call validity measurement was taken for v1.1.4 (200/200 on two aliases); it is repeated for this candidate in the rc notes.\nv1/\nv1.1.2/\n/usr/bin/grep: docs/RELEASE_PROCESS.md: No such file or directory","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8a735a95-b244-4e7c-a13d-5577584d6ea7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
