{"parentUuid":"0cb3a4e2-3fb2-44a9-ad7f-9505f38db53b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch4L57MtMC8zEjC9W78WZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mvked7VxmZ3z6Wt7UJqyUP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/scratchpad/g120/out; D=/home/mike/nexus-wt/v120-evidence/docs/evidence/v1.2.0; cp $S/attempt1/wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.json $D/wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.attempt1-pool-outage.json && (cd $D && sha256sum wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.attempt1-pool-outage.json > wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.attempt1-pool-outage.json.sha256) && cat > $D/G1.1-4-rc.1.md <<'EOF'\n# G1.1-4 on v1.2.0-rc.1: live tool-call validity (not met)\n\n**Result: not met.** `engineering/deep` 200/200 native valid; `engineering/lead-reasoning` 195/200 (97.5%) against the 99.5% bar. The owner accepted promoting v1.2.0 with this recorded as a known limitation on 2026-11-15; this page is that record. Nothing here is independent qualification.\n\n- Candidate: `v1.2.0-rc.1`, commit `cc82b5ee6b4e798b4c76fbec62ab874bea9330cf`, tree `0ebd3543324bfae011803dd08d70ab1ad941a2ed`, archive sha256 `5cc1b6fb24842d5853e3db25c3e7e8588066333fba7552487deaf7cdc2ffe530`, installed from the release with attestation verification.\n- Provider: the shared gateway only (`gateway-openai-chat`, `temperature 0`, `max_tokens 8192`, response cache bypassed, 1200 ms request interval). Runner: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` from the candidate checkout, unmodified.\n- Client code on the request path (`client.ts`, `core/content_tool_call.ts`, the protocol adapters, `providers.ts`) and `eval/` are byte-identical between `v1.1.4` and `v1.2.0-rc.1`.\n\n## Runs (all kept)\n\n| Run | Result file | `deep` | `lead-reasoning` | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.attempt1-pool-outage.json` (sha256 `4e0344c6587704c6ee12380d26a1f8a3c586a05760c8d0e1d7923da035f1c9a2`) | 200/200 | 122/200 | 03:33Z start. Every `lead-reasoning` request after 04:24:07Z failed; probes at 04:27Z, 04:29Z returned HTTP 503 `pool_unavailable` (no healthy worker in pool `lead`). Gateway outage; not a measure of the client. |\n| 2 | not written | 200/200 (receipts) | 200 completed, 5 failed (receipts) | The runner could not write its result (`EEXIST`: the output path still held run 1's file, an operator error). Receipts sha256 `992639580c22376293c7ccbdb5925ef523cfb1bbba07fd4cc6377094c59cd1d9`. Not counted as a pass. |\n| 3 | `wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.json` (sha256 `b261191545f1e868c52a8e4a09aee6e9043fb22cf5c81020616a5f49981573af`) | 200/200 | **195/200** | 05:58Z start, `passed:false`. Receipts sha256 `461c1c5bc2587f4c708efc94b4b8b91a46fd99de387ecb991910fe9dc84f06c5`. This is the recorded result. |\n\n## What the five failures are\n\nAll five are `edit_file` attempts (45/50) at the same positions in runs 2 and 3: the five \"hybrid\" prompts that end \"Think before the call and emit a non-empty `<think>...</think>` block.\" Each ended as a 120 s client first-byte timeout (`failureKind: timeout` in the receipts). The other tools, and the non-hybrid `edit_file` prompts, were all valid.\n\nDiagnostics on the same alias, under the GATEWAY claim:\n\n- The plain `edit_file` prompt: 8/8 native valid, about 12.6 s each.\n- Five hybrid `edit_file` prompts followed by plain ones, client timeout raised to 200 s: the five hybrid calls each ended `finish_reason=length` (\"Model output was truncated; refusing to treat it as a complete answer\"), the plain ones were native valid.\n- The hybrid prompt sent directly with `tool_choice: \"required\"` and with `\"auto\"`: HTTP 200 after about 141 s, `finish_reason=length`, 8192 completion tokens, about 27,000 characters of reasoning, no tool call, in all 4 calls observed. Forcing the tool call does not change it.\n\nSo the model behind `engineering/lead-reasoning` reasons to the output cap on this prompt without calling the tool. The client correctly refuses to treat a truncated reply as an answer.\n\n## Why this is recorded as a limitation and not as a client defect\n\n- The same prompt class failed on the earlier `v1.1.4` run (`wp-1107-provider-matrix.json`: `lead-reasoning` 195/200, with `write_file` hybrid 0/5), and `v1.1.4-rc.2` then passed 200/200 (five forced retries) with the same client code. The outcome moves with the model's behaviour on that prompt, not with the client.\n- It was not fixed by changing the matrix, the prompts, the timeouts or the pass bar, and no workaround for this gateway's model was added to the product (the gateway is outside the product's control).\n- It is **not** claimed that the 99.5% bar is met for this build. A passing rerun of rc.1 would supersede run 3; none was obtained.\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- v1.2.1 unit MQ-0 carries the measurement forward; whether a reasoning-capable model that runs to the output cap on a \"think first\" prompt should be handled by the client (for example a per-request reasoning budget) is a product question for v1.2.1, not settled here.\nEOF\ncd /home/mike/nexus-wt/v120-evidence && ls docs/evidence/v1.2.0","description":"Write evidence record for rc.1 matrix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":818,"cache_read_input_tokens":211598,"output_tokens":2348,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":99},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":818,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2348,"cache_read_input_tokens":211598,"cache_creation_input_tokens":818,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":818},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"toolInputStreamMs":18415,"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Mvked7VxmZ3z6Wt7UJqyUP":{"command":"S=/tmp/claude-1000/-home-mike-nexus-code/6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68/scratchpad/g120/out; D=/home/mike/nexus-wt/v120-evidence/docs/evidence/v1.2.0; cp $S/attempt1/wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.json $D/wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.attempt1-pool-outage.json && (cd $D && sha256sum wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.attempt1-pool-outage.json > wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.attempt1-pool-outage.json.sha256) && cat > $D/G1.1-4-rc.1.md <<'EOF'\n# G1.1-4 on v1.2.0-rc.1: live tool-call validity (not met)\n\n**Result: not met.** `engineering/deep` 200/200 native valid; `engineering/lead-reasoning` 195/200 (97.5%) against the 99.5% bar. The owner accepted promoting v1.2.0 with this recorded as a known limitation on 2026-11-15; this page is that record. Nothing here is independent qualification.\n\n- Candidate: `v1.2.0-rc.1`, commit `cc82b5ee6b4e798b4c76fbec62ab874bea9330cf`, tree `0ebd3543324bfae011803dd08d70ab1ad941a2ed`, archive sha256 `5cc1b6fb24842d5853e3db25c3e7e8588066333fba7552487deaf7cdc2ffe530`, installed from the release with attestation verification.\n- Provider: the shared gateway only (`gateway-openai-chat`, `temperature 0`, `max_tokens 8192`, response cache bypassed, 1200 ms request interval). Runner: `eval/tool_grammar_matrix.mjs` from the candidate checkout, unmodified.\n- Client code on the request path (`client.ts`, `core/content_tool_call.ts`, the protocol adapters, `providers.ts`) and `eval/` are byte-identical between `v1.1.4` and `v1.2.0-rc.1`.\n\n## Runs (all kept)\n\n| Run | Result file | `deep` | `lead-reasoning` | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.attempt1-pool-outage.json` (sha256 `4e0344c6587704c6ee12380d26a1f8a3c586a05760c8d0e1d7923da035f1c9a2`) | 200/200 | 122/200 | 03:33Z start. Every `lead-reasoning` request after 04:24:07Z failed; probes at 04:27Z, 04:29Z returned HTTP 503 `pool_unavailable` (no healthy worker in pool `lead`). Gateway outage; not a measure of the client. |\n| 2 | not written | 200/200 (receipts) | 200 completed, 5 failed (receipts) | The runner could not write its result (`EEXIST`: the output path still held run 1's file, an operator error). Receipts sha256 `992639580c22376293c7ccbdb5925ef523cfb1bbba07fd4cc6377094c59cd1d9`. Not counted as a pass. |\n| 3 | `wp-1107-provider-matrix.rc.1.json` (sha256 `b261191545f1e868c52a8e4a09aee6e9043fb22cf5c81020616a5f49981573af`) | 200/200 | **195/200** | 05:58Z start, `passed:false`. Receipts sha256 `461c1c5bc2587f4c708efc94b4b8b91a46fd99de387ecb991910fe9dc84f06c5`. This is the recorded result. |\n\n## What the five failures are\n\nAll five are `edit_file` attempts (45/50) at the same positions in runs 2 and 3: the five \"hybrid\" prompts that end \"Think before the call and emit a non-empty `<think>...</think>` block.\" Each ended as a 120 s client first-byte timeout (`failureKind: timeout` in the receipts). The other tools, and the non-hybrid `edit_file` prompts, were all valid.\n\nDiagnostics on the same alias, under the GATEWAY claim:\n\n- The plain `edit_file` prompt: 8/8 native valid, about 12.6 s each.\n- Five hybrid `edit_file` prompts followed by plain ones, client timeout raised to 200 s: the five hybrid calls each ended `finish_reason=length` (\"Model output was truncated; refusing to treat it as a complete answer\"), the plain ones were native valid.\n- The hybrid prompt sent directly with `tool_choice: \"required\"` and with `\"auto\"`: HTTP 200 after about 141 s, `finish_reason=length`, 8192 completion tokens, about 27,000 characters of reasoning, no tool call, in all 4 calls observed. Forcing the tool call does not change it.\n\nSo the model behind `engineering/lead-reasoning` reasons to the output cap on this prompt without calling the tool. The client correctly refuses to treat a truncated reply as an answer.\n\n## Why this is recorded as a limitation and not as a client defect\n\n- The same prompt class failed on the earlier `v1.1.4` run (`wp-1107-provider-matrix.json`: `lead-reasoning` 195/200, with `write_file` hybrid 0/5), and `v1.1.4-rc.2` then passed 200/200 (five forced retries) with the same client code. The outcome moves with the model's behaviour on that prompt, not with the client.\n- It was not fixed by changing the matrix, the prompts, the timeouts or the pass bar, and no workaround for this gateway's model was added to the product (the gateway is outside the product's control).\n- It is **not** claimed that the 99.5% bar is met for this build. A passing rerun of rc.1 would supersede run 3; none was obtained.\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- v1.2.1 unit MQ-0 carries the measurement forward; whether a reasoning-capable model that runs to the output cap on a \"think first\" prompt should be handled by the client (for example a per-request reasoning budget) is a product question for v1.2.1, not settled here.\nEOF\ncd /home/mike/nexus-wt/v120-evidence && ls docs/evidence/v1.2.0","description":"Write evidence record for rc.1 matrix"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Ch4L574nArydj4BnxDoJb","requestRef":"0d29d1ec-b88c-456b-9618-67019d1f9a48","requestedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","promptCacheRequested":"1h","attributionSkill":"loop","type":"assistant","uuid":"100ed27c-4d59-4c82-b237-3891426a9feb","timestamp":"2026-11-15T07:36:32.533Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/mike/nexus-code","sessionId":"6473a60e-9fa2-4bd9-9d0c-35324295cf68","version":"2.1.323","gitBranch":"main","slug":"robust-rolling-otter"}
